{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation: confirmed the AnyIO behavior the blocker questioned on the pinned worktree dependency. With the default limiter reduced to one token, abandon_on_cancel=False leaves the canceled caller alive with borrowed_tokens=1 and a later run_sync times out; abandon_on_cancel=True makes the caller exit, borrowed_tokens returns to 0, and the later quick call obtains capacity while the abandoned body is still blocked. Updated the plan/ACs to state this observable budget and the caller-gone discard contract."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788893979110227001,"uuid":"a0820877-694c-4028-b200-84e34f08b297"}